From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bastiaan van der Plaat <bastiaan.v.d.plaat@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 18:36:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Implement Mutex, Condvar and thread parking without SRW locks
 on Windows XP

Windows XP has no SRW locks, condition variables or WaitOnAddress. The
mutex waits on keyed events, which Windows XP has. Keyed events can't
wait with a timeout there: Windows XP can give a release to a wait that
times out at the same time, which then reports the timeout. So the thread
parker waits on an auto-reset event of its own, and the condition
variable queues the waiting threads, which park until a notify takes
them.
